  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 8404.01 Processing Application",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 8404.01 Processing Application.\n\n(a) Within 30 days of receiving an application, the director shall review the application and notify the applicant of any apparent errors or missing information.\n\n(b) An application shall be granted if the director determines that the requirements set forth in Saf-C 8403.01(b)-(d) and Saf-C 8403.02 have been satisfied.\n\n(c) An application shall be denied if the director determines that any of the requirements set forth in Saf-C 8403.01(b)-(d) and Saf-C 8403.02 are not met. If an application is denied, the director shall state in writing the reason(s) for the denial and return the application to the applicant.\n\n(d) Any applicant whose application is denied may submit an application at any time.\n\n(e) Within 60 days of receiving an application or receiving an applicant’s response to the director’s notification in Saf-C 8404.01(a), the director shall notify the applicant whether the application is granted or denied.\n\nSource. #14340, eff 8-14-25, EXPIRES: 8-14-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c8400.html"
